May 2008 Dear Customer, Halifax Bank has been under severe spamming and phishing attacks in the last few weeks. Consequently, we are upgrading our servers to withstand these drastic surge of cyberattacks. Furthermore, we are introducing an additional security feature in our online banking service. Due to these vital technical upgrades, you may experience interruptions while using our online banking. To prevent this, update your online banking profile by clicking the link below: https://secure.halifax-online.co.uk/ NOTE: For security reasons, you will be required to provide your User ID, Password and other relevant information. Please ensure that you enter them accurately to avoid online banking access termination. We appreciate your understanding and apologize for any inconvenience. Lynne Bentley Head of Online Banking Security Halifax Bank plc As outlined in our User Agreement, Halifax Bank will periodically send you information about site changes and enhancements. Visit our Privacy Policy and User Agreement if you have any questions. Halifax is a division of Bank of Scotland plc. Registered in Scotland No. SC327000. Registered Office: The Mound, Edinburgh, EH1 1YZ",d14,Technology and IT Services,"GENERAL SETTINGS
